<h1>oracle Turing machine</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="turingMachine.html"><em>Turing machine</em></a> with an extra <a href="oracletape.html"><em>oracle tape</em></a> and three extra states q<sub>?</sub>, q<sub>y</sub>, q<sub>n</sub>.  When the machine enters q<sub>?</sub>, control goes to state q<sub>y</sub> if the oracle tape content is in the <a href="oracleset.html"><em>oracle set</em></a>; otherwise control goes to state q<sub>n</sub>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="alternatngTr.html"><em>alternating Turing machine</em></a>, <a href="nondetermTuringMach.html"><em>nondeterministic Turing machine</em></a>, <a href="probablturng.html"><em>probabilistic Turing machine</em></a>, <a href="universalTur.html"><em>universal Turing machine</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
